        <!-- FAQ Section -->
        <section class="mt-16 bg-zinc-900/60 rounded-xl p-8 border border-zinc-800">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-zinc-300">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">What is the mid-market exchange rate?</h3>
              <p class="text-zinc-400">The mid-market rate is the midpoint between the buy and sell prices of two currencies on the global foreign exchange market. It's considered the "real" exchange rate because it has no markup added by banks or payment providers.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Why does my bank's exchange rate differ from online converters?</h3>
              <p class="text-zinc-400">Banks and money transfer services add a margin (spread) to the mid-market rate as their profit. They may also charge flat fees. The rate you see on Google or our currency converter is the raw market rate without markup.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">How often do exchange rates change?</h3>
              <p class="text-zinc-400">Exchange rates fluctuate constantly — 24 hours a day, five days a week — based on supply and demand, interest rates, inflation, political events, and economic data releases. Major currencies can move 1–2% in a single day during volatile periods.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Is it better to convert currency at home or abroad?</h3>
              <p class="text-zinc-400">Generally, it's better to withdraw local currency from an ATM at your destination using a debit card with no foreign transaction fees. Airport exchanges and hotel desks almost always offer the worst rates. Use our currency converter to check the rate before you travel so you know what to expect.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <BlogShare url="https://solverspro.com/blog/how-to-convert-currency-accurately" title="How to Convert Currency Accurately: A Practical Guide for Travel, Business, and Investing" />
